module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.ONan.MatrixGenerators

/-!
# An eight-dimensional row-space witness for the O'Nan local subgroup

The displayed 8 by 45 matrix has an identity block in its first eight columns.
Right multiplication by each local subgroup word preserves its row space: the
two identities below give explicit 8 by 8 matrices acting on its rows. The
calculations use the published linear generators, so the invariant row space
also survives passage to the projective group.

The basis was found using GAP's MeatAxe on the ATLAS matrices. That computation
is only a producer of data: all identities here are checked by Lean's kernel,
using intermediate row matrices to avoid recomputing long products. Source
matrices and attribution: `refs/original/onan/README.md`. Subgroup words:
`ProjectiveOrder/source/README.md`. Orbit size is not asserted in this module.
-/

namespace ONan.OrderCertificate

set_option maxRecDepth 4096
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

-- Specify entrywise decisions explicitly, avoiding dependent instance search
-- through the large intermediate tables.
private def entryDecidable {m n : Nat} (M N : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) (ZMod 7)) :
    Decidable (∀ i j, M i j = N i j) :=
  @Nat.decidableForallFin m _ (fun i =>
    @Nat.decidableForallFin n _ (fun j => ZMod.decidableEq 7 (M i j) (N i j)))

